      analogy: "Imagine waiting at home for an urgent package delivery. Polling is like walking to your front door every 30 seconds, swinging it open, looking down at the empty porch, and walking back to your couch—you cannot focus on reading a book because your life is trapped in a checking loop. Interrupt-driven execution is like sitting on the couch reading a book comfortably until a loud doorbell rings (The Hardware Interrupt). You drop a bookmark, stand up, sign for the package (Execute the ISR), and sit back down to resume reading exactly where Bhuvana left off."
