      analogy: "Imagine two poker players sitting across from each other at a table, connected by a mechanical conveyor belt system driven by a foot pedal under the Master player's control. Every time the Master presses the foot pedal (The Clock Pulse on SCLK), the conveyor moves forward by one slot. A card shifts off the edge of the Master’s stack into the Slave’s hand (MOSI), while the exact same motion pushes a card off the edge of the Slave's stack straight into the Master's hand (MISO). It is a highly synchronized, continuous, two-way trade."
