      analogy: "Imagine running a busy city taxi dispatch center. Without a thread pool, every single time a citizen calls asking for a ride, you build a factory from scratch, manufacture a brand-new car, hire a new driver, send them out for one trip, and crush the car in a trash compactor the second the passenger hops out. This is madness. A Thread Pool is like keeping a permanent fleet of 50 active taxis sitting in a staging parking lot. When a ride request lands in the dispatch queue, an idle driver starts their engine, fulfills the request, and drives straight back to the lot to wait for the next passenger."
