      analogy: "Singleton: Think of an office building's central master printing machine. You don't want every employee to spawn a separate physical printer layout on their desks, which would drain budget resources. Instead, everyone shares access to a single, globally tracked master device pointer. The double-checked lock is like a security checkpoint: employees sprint down the hall; if they see the printer is already built, they walk back without slowing down.\nBuilder: Imagine ordering a highly customized gourmet sandwich at a digital kiosk display panel. Instead of shouting a massive, 20-item un-ordered instruction sentence at a confused chef, you use a fluid step-by-step assembly interface chain: .addBread('Rye').addMeat('Turkey').addCheese('Swiss').build(). The kiosk organizes your selections into a clean, deterministic manifest before launching construction."
